@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il03-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-120b-indexation`
IMPORT `ito-121-individual-rates`
IMPORT `ito-121b-additional-tax`
IMPORT `ito-il26-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il26-schedule-a`
IMPORT `ito-il26-regulations`
IMPORT `ito-il26-s164`
IMPORT `ito-il26-claims`
IMPORT `ito-il26-published-figures`

-- Tests for s 164 and the Deduction from Salary and Wages Regulations 5753-1993. Every expected value was worked
-- out BY HAND from the rates and figures the sources print (the arithmetic is written beside each group) before
-- the assertion was run. None was copied from an evaluation. A failing assertion here is a finding about the
-- source or the encoding, never a value to edit.
--
-- THE FIGURES USED, and which of them is law:
--   * the s 121 scale for 2026-2027, as the Ordinance prints it (ITO s 121(a), (b)(1)): 10% to 84,120; 14% to
--     120,720; 20% to 228,000; 31% to 301,200; 35% to 560,280; 47% above. Cumulative tax at the tops of the bands:
--       84,120 x 10%                                 =   8,412
--       + (120,720 - 84,120) = 36,600 x 14% = 5,124  =  13,536
--       + (228,000 - 120,720) = 107,280 x 20% = 21,456 = 34,992
--       + (301,200 - 228,000) = 73,200 x 31% = 22,692  = 57,684
--       + (560,280 - 301,200) = 259,080 x 35% = 90,678 = 148,362
--     A salary is income from personal exertion, so the reduced rates of s 121(b)(1) apply to it up to 301,200.
--   * s 121B(a): 3% of the part of the taxable income over 721,560 (the Tax Authority's figure for 2026, carried
--     for 2027 by s 120B(e)(1)). NOT law in this file: the published figure.
--   * the credit point, NIS 2,904 a year (the Tax Authority's figure for 2025, carried for 2026-2027 by
--     s 120B(e)(1)); 2.25 credit points = 6,534. The 2.25 is a number a test employee declares, not a computed
--     entitlement.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `The employee's declarations`
`an employee born in 1990 with a card, claiming credit points:` p MEANS
    `The employee's declarations` WITH
        `gave the employer an employee's card (form 0101)`                                    IS TRUE
        `filled in the section of the card on other income`                                    IS TRUE
        `declared on the card an additional position, or a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE
        `declared on form 0130 that there is no other taxable income`                          IS FALSE
        `told the employer of other taxable income after making that declaration`              IS FALSE
        `credit points claimed on the card`                                                    IS p
        `date of birth`                                                                        IS YMD 1990 1 1

GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A payment of salary`
`a full-time monthly salary of` s `in` y MEANS
    `A payment of salary` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                       IS y
        `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                      IS y
        `the month's salary`                                                             IS s
        `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                            IS s
        `days worked in the month`                                                       IS 22
        `hours worked a day`                                                             IS 8
        `hours worked a week`                                                            IS 40
        `the payment is a pension`                                                       IS FALSE
        `the employee is a foreign worker`                                               IS FALSE
        `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE


-- Variants of the standard employee and of the standard payment, one named constant each (a record is built
-- whole; the language has no update of a field).

