        `the salary`  IS `declined where the order of rounding changes the tax`
        `the share`   IS `the share is rounded as item (5) of Schedule A rounds a tax`
        `the amounts` IS `declined where the year changes the tax`
        `the placing` IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`
        `the age`     IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested`

`the readings, share exact` MEANS
    `The readings of the withholding rules` WITH
        `the set-off` IS `declined where the object of the set-off changes the tax`
        `the salary`  IS `declined where the order of rounding changes the tax`
        `the share`   IS `the share is exact`
        `the amounts` IS `declined where the year changes the tax`
        `the placing` IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`
        `the age`     IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested`

`figures supplied by hand` MEANS
    `The annual figures for the tax year` WITH
        `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` IS 721_560
        `the value of one credit point` IS 2_904

`the 2026 figures` MEANS `the annual figures published for tax year` 2026
`the readings by default` MEANS `the readings of the withholding rules, by default`

-- The withholding on a salary of s in 2026 for an employee born in 1990 claiming p points, readings by default.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
      p IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the payment, for the withholding rules` NUMBER
`the 2026 withholding on` s `with credit points:` p MEANS
    `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` s `in` 2026) `given` (`an employee born in 1990 with a card, claiming credit points:` p) `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction`

-- The same, with a given reading, so that a fork can be tested by name.
GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
      p IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `The readings of the withholding rules`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the payment, for the withholding rules` NUMBER
`the 2026 withholding on` s `with credit points:` p `, reading` r MEANS
    `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` s `in` 2026) `given` (`an employee born in 1990 with a card, claiming credit points:` p) `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` r `under the direction` `no direction`

§§ `Schedule A — a monthly salary, 2.25 credit points (6,534 a year), readings by default`

-- A1: 10,000 x 12 = 120,000. Tax = 8,412 + (120,000 - 84,120) x 14% = 8,412 + 35,880 x 14% = 8,412 + 5,023.20 = 13,435.20.
--     Less 6,534 = 6,901.20. / 12 = 575.10. A fraction of 0.10 is not over 49 agorot: 575.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 10_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 575

-- A2: 20,000 x 12 = 240,000. Tax = 34,992 + (240,000 - 228,000) x 31% = 34,992 + 3,720 = 38,712.
--     Less 6,534 = 32,178. / 12 = 2,681.50. A fraction of exactly 50 agorot is over 49: 2,682.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 20_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 2_682

-- A3: 4,000 x 12 = 48,000. Tax = 4,800 (10%). Less 6,534 = -1,734: the credit exceeds the tax, so nothing is
--     deducted (a credit point is set off against the tax, never into a refund; assumption A1 in NOTES).
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 4_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 0

-- A4-A6: the point where the tax equals the credits. 10% band: 12 x S x 10% = 6,534 at S = 5,445.
--     S = 5,445: tax 6,534; less 6,534 = 0; 0.
--     S = 5,449: 65,388 x 10% = 6,538.80; less 6,534 = 4.80; / 12 = 0.40; not over 49 agorot: 0.
--     S = 5,450: 65,400 x 10% = 6,540; less 6,534 = 6; / 12 = 0.50; over 49 agorot: 1.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 5_445 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 5_449 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 5_450 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 1

-- A7: 50,000 x 12 = 600,000. Tax = 148,362 + (600,000 - 560,280) x 47% = 148,362 + 39,720 x 47% = 148,362 + 18,668.40
--     = 167,030.40. Less 6,534 = 160,496.40. / 12 = 13,374.70. A fraction of 70 agorot: 13,375.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 50_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 13_375

-- A8: 60,130 x 12 = 721,560, the s 121B(a) amount: not exceeded, no additional tax.
--     Tax = 148,362 + (721,560 - 560,280) x 47% = 148,362 + 161,280 x 47% = 148,362 + 75,801.60 = 224,163.60.
--     Less 6,534 = 217,629.60. / 12 = 18,135.80: 18,136.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 60_130 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 18_136

-- A9: 61,000 x 12 = 732,000. Tax = 148,362 + (732,000 - 560,280) x 47% = 148,362 + 171,720 x 47% = 148,362 + 80,708.40
--     = 229,070.40. Additional tax 3% x (732,000 - 721,560) = 3% x 10,440 = 313.20. Total 229,383.60.
--     Less 6,534 = 222,849.60. / 12 = 18,570.80: 18,571. (Without s 121B it would be 222,536.40 / 12 = 18,544.70: 18,545.)
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 61_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 18_571

-- A10: 70,000 x 12 = 840,000. Tax = 148,362 + (840,000 - 560,280) x 47% = 148,362 + 279,720 x 47% = 148,362 + 131,468.40
--     = 279,830.40. Additional tax 3% x (840,000 - 721,560) = 3% x 118,440 = 3,553.20. Total 283,383.60.
--     Less 6,534 = 276,849.60. / 12 = 23,070.80: 23,071.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 EQUALS RIGHT 23_071

-- A11: no credit points. 10,000: 13,435.20 / 12 = 1,119.60: 1,120.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 10_000 `with credit points:` 0 EQUALS RIGHT 1_120

-- A12: 2.75 points = 2.75 x 2,904 = 7,986. 10,000: 13,435.20 - 7,986 = 5,449.20. / 12 = 454.10: 454.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 10_000 `with credit points:` 2.75 EQUALS RIGHT 454

§§ `Schedule A — both sides of each band of s 121, no credit points`

