§§ `Schedule A — the tax year, and the age of the employee`

-- 2027 prints the same ceilings and the same credit point (s 120B(e)(1)): 10,000 with 2.25 points is 575 as in 2026.
#ASSERT `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` 10_000 `in` 2027) `given` `the standard employee` `with` (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2027) `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
-- Born 1960 (66 in 2026): the salary is income from personal exertion, so the reduced rates apply under (b)(1) at any
-- age, and the day on which the age of 60 is tested (IL-03 fork F2) does not change the tax. 575 again, by default.
#ASSERT `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` 10_000 `in` 2026) `given` `the standard employee, born in 1960` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
-- 2025 and 2028: section 121 is not answered by IL-03's text for them (2025: before the 2026 amendment; 2028: s 120B(e)(2)).
-- The published-figures function refuses first; with the figures supplied by hand the refusal is IL-03's.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the annual figures published for tax year` 2025 BECAUSE "no annual figures published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year have been sourced in this encoding"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the annual figures published for tax year` 2028 BECAUSE "no annual figures published by the Israel Tax Authority for this tax year have been sourced in this encoding"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` 10_000 `in` 2025) `given` `the standard employee` `with` `figures supplied by hand` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding on` (`a full-time monthly salary of` 10_000 `in` 2028) `given` `the standard employee` `with` `figures supplied by hand` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` BECAUSE "the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text"
-- The figures module carries the Authority's numbers through s 120B(e)(1) to the two years.
#ASSERT (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2026)'s `the value of one credit point` EQUALS 2_904
#ASSERT (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2027)'s `the value of one credit point` EQUALS 2_904
#ASSERT (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2026)'s `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` EQUALS 721_560
#ASSERT (`the annual figures published for tax year` 2027)'s `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` EQUALS 721_560

