-- Salary 1,234.90. Rounded first: 1,235 x 12 = 14,820; 10% = 1,482; / 12 = 123.50: 124.
--                  As it stands:  1,234.90 x 12 = 14,818.80; 10% = 1,481.88; / 12 = 123.49: 123.   They part.
-- Salary 1,234.40. Rounded first: 1,234 -> 123.40: 123.   As it stands: 123.44: 123.   They agree.
-- Salary 1,234.95. Rounded first: 1,235 -> 123.50: 124.   As it stands: 123.495: 124.  They agree.
-- Salary 1,234.50. Rounded first: 1,235 -> 123.50: 124.   As it stands: 123.45: 123.   They part.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.9 `with credit points:` 0 `, reading` `the readings, salary rounded first` EQUALS RIGHT 124
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.9 `with credit points:` 0 `, reading` `the readings, only the tax rounded` EQUALS RIGHT 123
#ASSERT REFUSED `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.9 `with credit points:` 0 BECAUSE "Schedule A item (5) rounds a fraction of a shekel from the salary or from the tax and does not say whether the salary is rounded before it is multiplied by 12; the two readings give different tax here"
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.4 `with credit points:` 0 EQUALS RIGHT 123
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.95 `with credit points:` 0 EQUALS RIGHT 124
