#ASSERT REFUSED `the 2026 withholding on` 1_234.5 `with credit points:` 0 BECAUSE "Schedule A item (5) rounds a fraction of a shekel from the salary or from the tax and does not say whether the salary is rounded before it is multiplied by 12; the two readings give different tax here"

§§ `Fork F1 — what the credit points are set off against (item 3)`

-- 70,000 a month with 100 points: credits 100 x 2,904 = 290,400. s 121 tax 279,830.40 (A10), s 121B tax 3,553.20.
--   Against the whole: 279,830.40 + 3,553.20 - 290,400 = -7,016.40, not below nil: 0.        / 12 = 0.
--   Against the s 121 tax only: 279,830.40 - 290,400 < 0 so 0; plus 3,553.20 = 3,553.20.      / 12 = 296.10: 296.
-- They part, so the default refuses. With 2.25 points (A10) the credits are below the s 121 tax and the readings agree.
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 100 `, reading` `the readings, set off against the whole` EQUALS RIGHT 0
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 100 `, reading` `the readings, set off against the s 121 tax only` EQUALS RIGHT 296
#ASSERT REFUSED `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 100 BECAUSE "Schedule A item (3) takes the credit points into account against the tax computed under ss 121 and 121B, and the text does not say whether the s 121B additional tax is reduced by them; the two readings give different tax here"
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 `, reading` `the readings, set off against the s 121 tax only` EQUALS RIGHT 23_071
#ASSERT `the 2026 withholding on` 70_000 `with credit points:` 2.25 `, reading` `the readings, set off against the whole` EQUALS RIGHT 23_071


§§ `Fork F4 — which year's amounts: a salary paid in one tax year for another`

-- 10,000 a month with 2.25 points is 575 in 2026 and in 2027 (the amounts are the same: s 120B(e)(1)).
--   Paid in 2027 for 2026: both years answer and agree: 575 by either reading and by default.
--   Paid in 2026 for 2025: the year of payment gives 575; the year of the work is a year the sources do not
--   answer (section 121 before 2026 is not in the deposited text); they part, so the default declines.
`a salary of 10,000 paid in 2027 for 2026` MEANS
    `A payment of salary` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                       IS 2027
        `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                      IS 2026
        `the month's salary`                                                             IS 10_000
        `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                            IS 10_000
        `days worked in the month`                                                       IS 22
        `hours worked a day`                                                             IS 8
        `hours worked a week`                                                            IS 40
        `the payment is a pension`                                                       IS FALSE
        `the employee is a foreign worker`                                               IS FALSE
        `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE

`a salary of 10,000 paid in 2026 for 2025` MEANS
    `A payment of salary` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                       IS 2026
        `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                      IS 2025
        `the month's salary`                                                             IS 10_000
        `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                            IS 10_000
        `days worked in the month`                                                       IS 22
        `hours worked a day`                                                             IS 8
        `hours worked a week`                                                            IS 40
        `the payment is a pension`                                                       IS FALSE
        `the employee is a foreign worker`                                               IS FALSE
        `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE

`the readings, the year of payment` MEANS
    `The readings of the withholding rules` WITH
        `the set-off` IS `declined where the object of the set-off changes the tax`
        `the salary`  IS `declined where the order of rounding changes the tax`
        `the share`   IS `declined where rounding the share changes the tax`
        `the placing` IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`
        `the age`     IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested`
        `the amounts` IS `the year in which the salary is paid`

`the readings, the year of the work` MEANS
    `The readings of the withholding rules` WITH
        `the set-off` IS `declined where the object of the set-off changes the tax`
        `the salary`  IS `declined where the order of rounding changes the tax`
        `the share`   IS `declined where rounding the share changes the tax`
        `the placing` IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale`
        `the age`     IS `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested`
        `the amounts` IS `the year for which the salary is paid`

`the 2027 figures` MEANS `the annual figures published for tax year` 2027

#ASSERT `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2027 for 2026` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2027 figures` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
#ASSERT `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2027 for 2026` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2027 figures` `reading` `the readings, the year of payment` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
#ASSERT `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2027 for 2026` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2027 figures` `reading` `the readings, the year of the work` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
#ASSERT `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2026 for 2025` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings, the year of payment` `under the direction` `no direction` EQUALS RIGHT 575
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2026 for 2025` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings, the year of the work` `under the direction` `no direction` BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"
-- (First written with the expectation that the refusal would be the figures module's, "no annual figures published ... for
-- this tax year". It is section 121's, which Schedule A reaches first; the figures are read only by s 121B. The expected
-- OUTCOME, a refusal for 2025, was right and is unchanged; only the name of the refusal was mis-predicted. NOTES.md, finding W1.)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding on` `a salary of 10,000 paid in 2026 for 2025` `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction` BECAUSE "Schedule A item (2) takes the section 120B adjustments without saying whether a salary paid in one tax year for another is deducted by the amounts of the year in which it is paid or of the year for which it is paid; the two readings give different answers here"

§§ `Regulation 3(b) — a month's salary paid in parts (fork F3)`

-- 20,000 a month, 2.25 points: the whole month's tax is 2,682 (A2).
--   A part of 12,000 (0.6): 2,682 x 0.6 = 1,609.20; rounded 1,609.   They part.
--   A part of  8,000 (0.4): 2,682 x 0.4 = 1,072.80; rounded 1,073.   They part.
--   A part of 10,000 (0.5): 2,682 x 0.5 = 1,341 exactly.             They agree.
--   The whole 20,000: 2,682.
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A payment of salary`
`a monthly salary of 20,000, the part paid being:` part MEANS
    `A payment of salary` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                       IS 2026
        `the tax year for which the salary is paid`                                      IS 2026
        `the month's salary`                                                             IS 20_000
        `the part of the month's salary paid in this payment`                            IS part
        `days worked in the month`                                                       IS 22
        `hours worked a day`                                                             IS 8
        `hours worked a week`                                                            IS 40
        `the payment is a pension`                                                       IS FALSE
        `the employee is a foreign worker`                                               IS FALSE
        `the employee works elsewhere, or receives a taxable pension from another payer` IS FALSE

GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      r IS A `The readings of the withholding rules`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the payment, for the withholding rules` NUMBER
`the withholding on a part of` part `reading` r MEANS
    `the withholding on` (`a monthly salary of 20,000, the part paid being:` part) `given` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` r `under the direction` `no direction`

#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 12_000 `reading` `the readings, share exact` EQUALS RIGHT 1_609.2
#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 12_000 `reading` `the readings, share rounded` EQUALS RIGHT 1_609
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding on a part of` 12_000 `reading` `the readings by default` BECAUSE "regulation 3(b) deducts a proportionate part of the tax on the month's salary and does not say whether that share is rounded to the shekel; the two readings give different tax here"
#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 8_000 `reading` `the readings, share exact` EQUALS RIGHT 1_072.8
#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 8_000 `reading` `the readings, share rounded` EQUALS RIGHT 1_073
#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 10_000 `reading` `the readings by default` EQUALS RIGHT 1_341
#ASSERT `the withholding on a part of` 20_000 `reading` `the readings by default` EQUALS RIGHT 2_682

§§ `Regulations 3(a) and 5 — which route a payment takes`

-- The maximal rate is the top rate of s 121: 47% (ITO s 121(a)(3)); not rounded (assumption A2).
GIVEN pay IS A `A payment of salary`
      decl IS AN `The employee's declarations`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the payment, for the withholding rules` NUMBER
`the withholding, 2026, by default, on` pay `given` decl MEANS
    `the withholding on` pay `given` decl `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings by default` `under the direction` `no direction`

-- M1: a partial salary (4 hours a day), no declaration on form 0130: 47% x 3,000 = 1,410.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a partial salary of 3,000` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 1_410
-- M2: the same with the form 0130 declaration: Schedule A. 3,000 x 12 = 36,000; tax 3,600; less 6,534: nil. 0.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a partial salary of 3,000` `given` `the standard employee with a form 0130 declaration` EQUALS RIGHT 0
-- M3: the declaration, but the employee has since told the employer of other taxable income (5(d)): 1,410 again.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a partial salary of 3,000` `given` `the standard employee with a form 0130 declaration, later told of other income` EQUALS RIGHT 1_410
-- M4: a pension of 8,000 (5(b)), no declaration: 47% x 8,000 = 3,760.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a pension of 8,000` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 3_760
-- M5: the same pension on the form 0130 declaration: Schedule A. 8,000 x 12 = 96,000; tax 8,412 + (96,000 - 84,120) x 14%
--     = 8,412 + 11,880 x 14% = 8,412 + 1,663.20 = 10,075.20; less 6,534 = 3,541.20; / 12 = 295.10: 295.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a pension of 8,000` `given` `the standard employee with a form 0130 declaration` EQUALS RIGHT 295
-- M6: no card given: 47% x 20,000 = 9,400. A card whose other-income section is empty: 9,400.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a monthly salary of 20,000` `given` `the standard employee who gave no card` EQUALS RIGHT 9_400
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a monthly salary of 20,000` `given` `the standard employee whose card has no other-income section` EQUALS RIGHT 9_400
-- M7: a salary for an additional position (6 hours a day, employed elsewhere) that the employee declared: 9,400.
--     Not declared: Schedule A, 2,682 (A2).
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for an additional position` `given` `the standard employee who declared an additional position` EQUALS RIGHT 9_400
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for an additional position` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 2_682
-- M8: more than 5 hours a day but fewer than 8 hours a week is a partial salary: 47% x 20,000 = 9,400.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for 6 hours a day and 7 a week` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 9_400
-- M9: 18 days a month is a month's work (Schedule A, 2,682); 17 days at 8 hours a day and 40 a week is a day employee (Schedule B).
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for 18 days` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 2_682
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for 17 days` `given` `the standard employee` BECAUSE "wages of a day employee are deducted under regulation 3(c) and Schedule B, which this row does not encode"
-- M10: 17 days but only 5 hours a week at 8 hours a day: fewer than 8 hours a week with more than 5 hours a day is a partial salary: 9,400.
#ASSERT `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 for 17 days and 5 hours a week` `given` `the standard employee` EQUALS RIGHT 9_400
-- M11: a foreign worker is regulation 3(d): declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the withholding, 2026, by default, on` `a salary of 20,000 to a foreign worker` `given` `the standard employee` BECAUSE "a salary to a foreign worker is deducted under regulation 3(d) and Schedule C (and regulation 11(d)), which this row does not encode"
-- M12: the maximal rate is declined for the years section 121 is not answered.
#ASSERT `the maximal rate in` 2026 EQUALS 47%
#ASSERT REFUSED `the maximal rate in` 2028 BECAUSE "the section 121 ceilings from tax year 2028 are not determined by the deposited text"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the maximal rate in` 2025 BECAUSE "section 121 as it stood before tax year 2026 is not in the deposited text"

