§§ `Regulation 4(a) — a non-regular salary`

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A non-regular salary`
`a non-regular salary of` b `, bankrupt:` bankrupt MEANS
    `A non-regular salary` WITH
        `amount` IS b
        `paid to the employees of a bankrupt or a company in liquidation` IS bankrupt

GIVEN b IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
      bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on a non-regular salary of` b `paid with` s `, bankrupt:` bankrupt MEANS
    `regulation 4(a) — the tax on` (`a non-regular salary of` b `, bankrupt:` bankrupt) `paid with a month's salary of` s `in` 2026 `for` `the standard employee` `with` `the 2026 figures` `reading` `the readings by default`

-- B1: salary 20,000 (tax 2,682), non-regular 24,000: a twelfth is 2,000. Tax on 22,000: 264,000 -> 34,992 + (264,000 - 228,000) x 31%
--     = 34,992 + 11,160 = 46,152; less 6,534 = 39,618; / 12 = 3,301.50: 3,302. Difference 3,302 - 2,682 = 620. x 12 = 7,440.
--     (Which is 31% x 24,000: the bonus falls wholly in the 31% band.)
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 24_000 `paid with` 20_000 `, bankrupt:` FALSE EQUALS 7_440
-- B2: non-regular 6,000: a twelfth 500. Tax on 20,500: 246,000 -> 34,992 + 18,000 x 31% = 40,572; less 6,534 = 34,038; / 12 = 2,836.50: 2,837.
--     Difference 2,837 - 2,682 = 155. x 12 = 1,860 (= 31% x 6,000).
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 6_000 `paid with` 20_000 `, bankrupt:` FALSE EQUALS 1_860
-- B3: nothing paid: no difference.
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 0 `paid with` 20_000 `, bankrupt:` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- B4: salary 5,000 (tax 60,000 x ... 6,000 less 6,534: nil -> 0), non-regular 12,000: a twelfth 1,000. Tax on 6,000: 72,000 x 10% = 7,200;
--     less 6,534 = 666; / 12 = 55.50: 56. Difference 56 - 0 = 56. x 12 = 672.
--     For the employees of a bankrupt the rate is not to be below 25%: 25% x 12,000 = 3,000 > 672, so 3,000.
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 12_000 `paid with` 5_000 `, bankrupt:` FALSE EQUALS 672
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 12_000 `paid with` 5_000 `, bankrupt:` TRUE  EQUALS 3_000
-- B5: for the bankrupt's employees where the tax is already above 25%: 7,440 (B1) against a floor of 25% x 24,000 = 6,000: 7,440.
#ASSERT `the tax on a non-regular salary of` 24_000 `paid with` 20_000 `, bankrupt:` TRUE EQUALS 7_440

§§ `Schedule A item (6) — the Director's table; and the cumulative method`

#ASSERT `the employer deducts, given the Director's table` (JUST 700) EQUALS 700
#ASSERT REFUSED `the employer deducts, given the Director's table` NOTHING BECAUSE "needs a source: Schedule A item (6) has the employer deduct by the table the Director publishes (the Tax Authority's monthly deduction booklet), which is not among the deposited sources; this encoding computes the tax of items (1) to (5), not the table"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a cumulative method of withholding` BECAUSE "needs a source: the text of the Regulations contains no cumulative method of withholding; the deposited sources do not say whether the Tax Authority prescribes one elsewhere"

§§ `The difference from the annual tax that row IL-03 computes`

-- An employee on 20,000 a month all year, 2.25 points. The annual tax under s 121 on 240,000 is 38,712 (A2); less the
-- credits 6,534 is 32,178. Twelve withholdings of 2,682 are 32,184, six shekels more: the difference is the rounding of
-- item (5) alone (2,681.50 rounded up twelve times), since the Schedule's calculation is the annual one divided by twelve.
#ASSERT `the tax under section 121 for` (`the individual earning` 240_000 `in` 2026 `born` (YMD 1990 1 1)) `, placing the eligible income as` `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of where the eligible income sits on the scale` `and testing the age of 60 as` `section 121(b)(1) — the reading this row takes of when the age of 60 is tested` EQUALS RIGHT 38_712
#ASSERT 12 TIMES 2_682 MINUS (38_712 MINUS 6_534) EQUALS 6

§§ `Section 164`

#ASSERT `section 164 imposes a duty to deduct tax when paying` `employment income, including the part of a retirement or death grant not exempt under section 9(7A)`
#ASSERT `section 164 imposes a duty to deduct tax when paying` `interest or dividend`
#ASSERT `section 164 applies to the State as a payer`
#ASSERT `the instrument prescribing the manner and rates of deduction from` `employment income, including the part of a retirement or death grant not exempt under section 9(7A)` EQUALS "the Income Tax (Deduction from Salary and Wages) Regulations 5753-1993"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the instrument prescribing the manner and rates of deduction from` `interest or dividend` BECAUSE "needs a source: section 164 leaves the manner and rates for this kind of payment to instruments (orders and regulations made under it) that are not among the deposited sources; only the Regulations for employment income are"

§§ `Regulations 2 and 9 — what the employee may claim`

#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 9(a) for` `being a new immigrant (section 35)` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 9(a) for` `professional liability insurance paid through the employer under a collective agreement` EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `the paragraph of regulation 9(a) for` `blindness, or a disability of 100% or of 90% on the special computation (section 9(5))` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the employee may ask the assessing officer to reduce the deduction on the ground` `credit points under section 40C or 40D`
-- Regulation 9(c): a pension of 10,000 of which 4,000 is exempt under s 9A or 9B: tax is deducted from 6,000.
#ASSERT `the part of a pension of` 10_000 `from which tax is deducted, the part exempt under section 9A or 9B being` 4_000 EQUALS 6_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the part of a pension of` 10_000 `from which tax is deducted, the part exempt under section 9A or 9B being` 10_001 BECAUSE "the exempt part of a pension exceeds the pension paid"
#ASSERT `the employer must demand an employee's card for` (`a full-time monthly salary of` 10_000 `in` 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must demand an employee's card for` `a salary of 10,000 to a foreign worker`
#ASSERT NOT `the employer must demand an employee's card for` `a salary of 10,000 for 10 days`
